Source landscape: The 2023 documentary universe is broad and includes federal budgets and economic surveys, BISP records, WHO/UNICEF/UNFPA/UNESCO assessments, World Bank human-capital and poverty work, flood-recovery reporting, education and health datasets, academic studies, and reputable local reporting. The strongest source families are official Pakistani records, multilateral assessments, household/outcome data, audits/evaluations, and independent reporting. Search coverage surfaced favorable, adverse, mixed, and contextual materials across welfare priority, service access, vulnerable groups, delivery capacity, crisis response, equality, and durable institutions. These are discovery leads only; they have not been inspected for evidence claims.

